  "rule": "Generated, not curated: a glyph superscripts iff Unicode defines a modifier letter whose compatibility decomposition is <super> of it. Exceptions ʔ→ˀ and ʕ→ˤ have no decomposition. Latin Extended-F forms (U+10780+, Unicode 14) are excluded — correct but near-universally tofu. One further exception: bare `g` is U+0067 for the plain-US constraint, but it stands for IPA ɡ (U+0261), so it superscripts to ᶢ (ɡ's form), not ᵍ."
 },
 "laws": {
  "optShift": [
   "Exclusivity, not duality: marks on the SAME dimension replace each other (`exclusive: true`); marks on INDEPENDENT dimensions stack. Tone level is a five-way scale (mid on ⌥a), so exclusive pairs need not be binary or exhaustive.",
   "⌥⇧ has three senses, not one: (a) the greater pole — ⌥= ⌥. ⌥w ⌥o ⌥q; (b) the more extreme value — ⌥e ⌥`; (c) the same glyph relocated below — ⌥n ⌥v ⌥u.",
   "Unpolarized duals (⌥s syllabic/non-syllabic, ⌥d apical/laminal) fall under none of the three: their shift assignment is arbitrary and is labelled as such."
  ],
  "keyClasses": [
   "IPA marks — earn a key by cross-tier phonetics (B), shape identity (C), or convention (A).",
   "Latin tenants — ⌥c cedilla, ⌥m ogonek, ⌥⇧x dot-below. No IPA meaning; kept so the layout can also type transliteration. They cohabit with IPA marks and are not pairs.",
   "Parked — no letter or shape claims them; assigned to mediocre reaches and labelled arbitrary rather than given a fake mnemonic. (⌥o, ⌥z, ⌥9, ⌥0)"
  ],
  "numberRow": "IPA *characters* with no Latin home — standalone glyphs (⇧2 ʔ, ⇧5 ə) and the tie bar ⇧1, which is a transformer, not an insertion."
 }
